From e947775cf7c6f984ee9a21074f6d655dcd969a2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:49:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: GIF arbiter rank, PSMCT24 chunk carry, pad snapshot

- GIF arbiter: one integer rank per packet (PATH1, PATH2, PATH3 in
  submission order, DIRECTHL behind queued PATH3 IMAGE data); the old
  comparator was not a strict weak ordering (UB in stable_sort) when a
  batch held PATH3 IMAGE, PATH3 non-image and DIRECTHL packets (review 55 G11).
- CPU GS backend: PSMCT24/Z24 host->local uploads carry the 0-2 bytes of a
  pixel that straddles an IMAGE chunk instead of dropping them (G14).
- Pad: the main thread samples raylib input after EndDrawing() and
  publishes a snapshot; the game thread no longer reads raylib state (G10).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
